    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37-a2">

                <pb facs="0056" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg50"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 38.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Otori to Mr.
                            Sill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Sill</hi>: I have the honor to acquaint you
                    that I have received a telegram from His Imperial Japanese Majesty’s minister
                    for foreign affairs that our legation and consulates, their archives, as well as
                    Japanese subjects in China, have been placed under the protection of the United
                    States, those legations and consulates having been withdrawn in consequence of
                    the cessation of peaceful relations between our country and China.</p>
                <p>Yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">K. Otori</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
